&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Goal: Drive business growth by identifying, developing, and closing new business opportunities across multiple sectors in the UK market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Responsibilities: Manage the entire sales cycle from lead generation to closing, maintain a strong sales pipeline, and mentor junior team members. You&#39;ll also attend networking events and collaborate with internal teams to provide the best solutions for clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: London, with a hybrid work setup (3 days in the office, 2 days remote).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Account Executive, you will be responsible for developing new business across multiple sectors. You&#39;ll work to understand client needs and provide a tailored Trustpilot solution for them. Your goal will be to develop and close new business while providing excellent client service. You will have experience selling a solution and demonstrate a strong track record of success in previous sales roles. We are looking for a creative sales professional with a passion for driving results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate new business opportunities with prospective clients by targeting all verticals in the UK market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full sales cycle, from lead generation and product demos to pricing, negotiation, and closing. Work with our sales development team to close a high percentage of new leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage a robust pipeline of relevant opportunities to meet and exceed sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain an in-depth understanding of our product by working closely with our in-house training team, pre-sales, management and your peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support junior Account Executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with Customer Success to ensure a smooth and professional handover happens between Trustpilot and the client&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend events to network and create leads, generating interest in the Trustpilot platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our marketing team to identify leads gathered from webinars and events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience selling complex Software as a Service (SaaS) solutions to senior decision makers is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to meet and exceed sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for building and maintaining strong client relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with sales metrics and how to use them to plan for growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to grow your skills whilst mentoring others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s in it for you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid work set up (3 days in our Central London office, 2 days WFH)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive base salary with an uncapped commission structure + company bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday per year, increasing to 28 days after 2 years of continuous employment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Two (paid) volunteering days a year to spend your time giving back to the causes that matter to you and your community&lt;/li&gt;
