&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Trustpilot, we&#39;re on an incredible journey. We&#39;re a profitable, high-growth FTSE-250 company with a big vision: to become the universal symbol of trust. We run the world&#39;s largest open customer review platform, and while we&#39;ve come a long way, there&#39;s still so much exciting work to do. Come join us at the heart of trust!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;64&quot;&gt;As our Senior Reward Analyst&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;94&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;you will join a close-knit Reward team, working cross-functionally with HR Business Partners, Talent Acquisition, Finance, and fellow &quot;Trusties&quot; to drive data-informed people decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;280&quot;&gt; Our mission is to deliver equitable, transparent, and market-competitive compensation and benefit programs that attract and retain top global talent. In this r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;430&quot;&gt;ole, you will tackle exciting challenges—from &lt;/span&gt;designing total reward dashboarding&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;530&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;leveraging compliant AI solutions&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;568&quot;&gt; to leading key annual review cycles, equity grants, and global market benchmarking.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;651&quot;&gt; You will also play a pivotal role in advancing our &lt;/span&gt;pay equity analysis, statutory gender pay gap reporting, and job architecture&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;781&quot;&gt;, directly reinforcing our commitment to an inclusive, transparent, and open-to-all workplace culture&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-start-index=&quot;882&quot;&gt;. If you are a collaborative data enthusiast eager to deliver impactful insights and elevate our global reward strategy, we would love to welcome you aboard.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze market data to inform compensation and benefit decisions that will enhance our ability to attract top talent across the countries the business operates&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date with market trends and legislation to advise identify risks and opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support/lead on activities required to deliver a well communicated and accurate annual salary review, bonus calculation, equity grants, benefits window and promotion cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance on budget modelling, cost analysis and scenario planning.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design of new/updated benefits, short term incentives and long term incentives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular pay equity analysis and support statutory gender pay gap reporting (EU, UK and any other applicable countries).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure reward practices comply with relevant employment and pay transparency regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain job architecture, levelling and job evaluation consistency across the organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain dashboarding to give leadership visibility on reward health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prove robust analysis on key reward topics (share dilution, range penetration, pay mix)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilise AI in a compliant way to deliver efficient solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with HR Business Partners and Talent Acquisition on reward topics to gain a deep understanding of the business needs and ensure they have the data and expert advice needed to make people decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and communicate clear and user friendly total reward communications and educational material (including ad hoc comms, cyclical communications, benefits communications and total reward statements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a reward role or associated discipline&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of key reward and HRIS processes and concepts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise working with people data and people systems / HRIS (currently Sage HR)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced spreadsheet skills with the ability to manipulate and analyse large volumes of data&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present complex data and insights in a clear, concise manner&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative mindset and ability to communicate cross-functionallyAbility to work autonomously and learn new skills and concepts rapidly&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A range of flexible working options to dedicate time to what matters to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation package + bonus&lt;/li&gt;
